# Virtual Reactor

A Python library for modeling, simulating, and optimizing chemical reactors.

## Project Vision

Virtual Reactor is a modular framework for developing mechanistic models of chemical reactors. The long-term goal is to achieve autodidactic insits in reactor modeling and perform gain training data for another AI Model.

## Current Status

The first implementation focuses on the classical Van de Vusse reaction in an ideal continuous stirred-tank reactor (CSTR).

## Planned Features

- Van de Vusse reaction network
- Isothermal CSTR
- Temperature-dependent kinetics
- Non-isothermal reactor model
- Parameter studies
- Automatic dataset generation
- Bayesian optimization
- Additional reactor types (Batch, PFR)

